    "https://saintleo.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/University-Campus/XMLNAME-2026-2027-FWS-Student-Worker--Student-Engagement---Leadership-Student-Assistant_R4678": {
      "title": "2026-2027 FWS Student Worker, Student Engagement & Leadership Student Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-04\nPart time\n\nJob Description Summary The Division of Student Affairs - Department of Student Engagement & Leadership Student Assistant provides comprehensive support for student engagement initiatives, event management, and family programming. This position supports the Department of Student Engagement & Leadership by assisting with event planning and execution, digital platform management, social media marketing, and direct student engagement activities while representing the university's mission and values. Job Description Please note: Hiring for this position is subject to funding availability and a limited number of openings. Applying does not guarantee employment. Primary Responsibilities:   Provide general support to the Department of Student Engagement & Leadership by assisting with day-to-day operations and special projects.  Welcome students, family members, faculty, staff, and community members using excellent customer service skills.  Positively represent Saint Leo University and the Department of Student Engagement & Leadership in all interactions.  Assist with comprehensive event management including planning, setup, execution, and tear-down for department programs and activities.  Manage and update the Lounge Platform to promote student engagement opportunities and track participation.  Handle email management tasks including correspondence, scheduling, and communication coordination.  Create and manage social media content across various platforms to promote department initiatives and events.  Develop marketing materials, flyers, and promotional content using design software and university branding guidelines.  Facilitate student engagement activities and serve as a liaison between students and department staff.  Manage and oversee bulletin boards, digital displays, and other promotional materials announcing events and programs.  Attend and assist with activities and events during evenings and weekends as assigned by department leadership.  Assist students, families, faculty, and staff with questions, concerns, and information requests.  Support the department leadership team with various administrative and programmatic projects.  Perform all other duties and responsibilities as assigned or directed by supervisors.  Qualifications:   Education/Experience   Strong oral and written communication skills in English are required.  Education or job experience in an office environment is a plus but not required.  Education or job experience in event planning, hospitality, student affairs, communications, marketing, and/or public relations is a plus, but not required.  Eligible to become Saint Leo University Van and Golf Cart Certified.  Knowledge, Skills, Abilities   Ability to communicate clearly, effectively, and professionally in spoken and written English.  The ability to speak and write in a second language is a plus but not required.  Ability to work effectively in an inclusive and professional environment.  Ability to work independently with minimal supervision and adapt to changing priorities.  Ability to multi-task and prioritize tasks to meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment.  Required proficiency in Microsoft Outlook, Word, and Excel for email management and administrative tasks.  Required proficiency in Canva for creating marketing materials and promotional content.  Intermediate proficiency in social media platforms (Instagram, Facebook, Twitter, etc.).  Experience with event planning and coordination software is a plus.  Detail-oriented with strong follow-up skills and ability to complete assigned projects.  Positive, pleasant attitude with excellent problem-solving abilities.  Professional attire required for special events and university functions.  Clean driving record and capability of driving University Vans.  Flexibility to work evenings and weekends as events require.   Ability to adapt to changing weekly schedules based on event calendar and department needs.   Minimum Qualifications:   Enrolled full-time at Saint Leo University in an Undergraduate Campus program.  Eligible for Federal Work Study funding.  Physical Demands:   The requirements listed below include physical abilities required to complete essential duties (e.g., ability to lift 50 lbs. using a hand truck)   Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.  ENVIRONMENT:   The work environment characteristics described here are a representation of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.  The term “qualified individual with a disability” means an individual with a disability who, with or without reasonable accommodation, can perform the essential functions of this position. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to communicate professionally in person, over the telephone, through email and other electronic means, move about the office and University, handle various type of media and equipment, and visually or otherwise identify, observe and assess.   The employee is occasionally required to lift up to 10 pounds unless otherwise specified in the job description. NOTICE: The intent of this job description is to provide a representation of the types of duties and responsibilities that will be required of positions given this title and shall not be construed as a declaration of the total specific duties and responsibilities of any particular position.  Employees may be directed to perform job-related tasks other than those specifically presented in this description.  Saint Leo University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and embraces diversity as a critical step in ensuring employee, student and graduate success.  Why Work at Saint Leo? What it’s Like to Work Here:  Ask our employees and the one word they’d use to describe working at Saint Leo University is “Community.” Our team members all share the Saint Leo core values, positive attitudes, and problem-solving abilities, enabling them to provide excellent student centered service. Our mission is educating and preparing students for life and leadership in a challenging world.  Thank you for your interest in joining the Saint Leo PRIDE! We are committed to providing our employees with the support they need. At Saint Leo, we offer an array of medical, dental, and vision packages as well as several add-on perks to make your benefits package truly customizable to you and your family needs. Available benefits based on employment status (Full Time vs Part Time). FREE Tuition - Employee, Spouse, and Dependents* Tuition Exchange Opportunity - Dependent of Employees* Generous Paid Leave - Sick, Vacation, and Holidays Comprehensive Group Health Plan (Medical, Dental, and Vision) Group Medical Plan includes Teledoc, Surgery Plus, Wellness Incentive Program and more! 100% Employer-Funded Health Reimbursement Account 100% Employer-Paid Short Term Disability Insurance 100% Employer-Funded Employee Assistance Program (healthcare and dependent options) Employer-provided life insurance Discounted On-Campus Dining Meal Plans Nationwide Pet Insurance Flexible Spending Accounts 403b Retirement Plan Wellness Center *Eligibility based on meeting required service period 2025 ICUBA Benefits Guide_St Leo"
    },
    "https://saintleo.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/University-Campus/Graduate-Assistant--Game-Operations_R6719": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant, Game Operations",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-11-02\nPart time\n\nJob Description Summary This individual will assist the Director of Game Day Operations & Events and will provide an opportunity to develop critical thinking skills through direct involvement in the oversight of game day operations and events. Job Description Duties and Tasks: Assist with facility set up for all home competitions, including special events. Assist in managing schedules for game operations student workers Learn specialized game operations roles such as scorekeeping, scoreboard, shot clock etc. Conducts athletic facility walk through and evaluation on regular basis for maintenance, safety and upkeep Researches and implements ideas to enhance branding, equipment, technology and environment at all facilities. Assist with golf cart maintenance and management Work with head coaches for game day planning and communication Manage storage areas in various facilities to maintain cleanliness Enter Facilities work orders for repairs, cleaning, etc. Assist with deliveries from vendors Other duties as assigned. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Knowledge: Bachelor’s degree from a regionally accredited college/university CPR/AED/First Aid certified or course completion within two months of employment Skills: Leadership skills Highly organized and attention to details Valid driver’s license Abilities: To be certified to drive university vehicles and assist with the functions of the athletic department motor pool including vans and golf carts. Ability to work in various weather conditions Ability to bend, stoop, twist, and lift up to 50 pounds ENVIRONMENT:   The work environment characteristics described here are a representation of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.  The term “qualified individual with a disability” means an individua