    "https://saintleo.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/University-Campus/Graduate-Assistant-Office-of-the-President_R6661": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant-Office of the President",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nPart time\n\nJob Description Summary The Graduate Assistant provides administrative and event support to the Office of the President at Saint Leo University, working directly with the Senior Executive to the President. The role combines secretarial work, event and meeting logistics, correspondence management, and backup coverage for the senior executive assistant. It offers graduate students’ close exposure to university leadership, governance, and institutional planning. The Graduate Assistant reports to the Senior Executive to the President. Discretion and confidentiality are a must. Job Description Duties and Tasks: Executive and secretarial support Provide secretarial support to the Senior Executive to the President Organize and efficiently process a large volume of correspondence from the President to various constituents. Arrange meetings and manage calendars, including tasks assigned by the Senior Executive to the President Substitute for the senior executive assistant in the President's office during her absence.   Events and meetings Work with the Senior Executive to the President to organize Strategic Planning, Key Result Areas (KRAs), Student Dinners, and other meetings or events assigned by the President. Oversee arrangements for Townhall and other Office of the President Events. Provide logistical support for the Office of the President events and meetings.   Board of Trustees Assist with Board of Trustees and board meeting preparations, as needed.   Student concerns Assist with student complaints by directing each to the appropriate contact before forwarding to the Senior Executive to the President.   Other duties Perform other duties as assigned by the Senior Executive to the President   Minimum Qualifications Enrollment in a graduate program at Saint Leo University in Business or a related field. A minimum 3.0 GPA in the graduate program, which must be maintained throughout the assistantship. Strong technology, analytical, and organizational skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite and website software, and familiarity with data analysis tools. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Self-starter who is highly motivated, with strong attention to detail, problem-solving skills, and the ability to identify and seek out information. Ability to manage competing priorities and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Must be discreet and always maintain strict confidentiality when handling sensitive or confidential information. .   Preferred Qualifications and Skills Previous academic or professional experience in business or technology-related roles. Experience in an executive office, higher education administration, or event coordination. Experience organizing meetings, events, or board-level activities. Strong customer service and interpersonal skills, with professionalism when working with trustees, donors, faculty, students, and community partners. Ability to route students concerns tactfully and to the right office.   Why Work at Saint Leo? What it’s Like to Work Here:  Ask our employees and the one word they’d use to describe working at Saint Leo University is “Community.” Our team members all share the Saint Leo core values, positive attitudes, and problem-solving abilities, enabling them to provide excellent student centered service. Our mission is educating and preparing students for life and leadership in a challenging world.  Thank you for your interest in joining the Saint Leo PRIDE! We are committed to providing our employees with the support they need. At Saint Leo, we offer an array of medical, dental, and vision packages as well as several add-on perks to make your benefits package truly customizable to you and your family needs. Available benefits based on employment status (Full Time vs Part Time). FREE Tuition - Employee, Spouse, and Dependents* Tuition Exchange Opportunity - Dependent of Employees* Generous Paid Leave - Sick, Vacation, and Holidays Comprehensive Group Health Plan (Medical, Dental, and Vision) Group Medical Plan includes Teledoc, Surgery Plus, Wellness Incentive Program and more! 100% Employer-Funded Health Reimbursement Account 100% Employer-Paid Short Term Disability Insurance 100% Employer-Funded Employee Assistance Program (healthcare and dependent options) Employer-provided life insurance Discounted On-Campus Dining Meal Plans Nationwide Pet Insurance Flexible Spending Accounts 403b Retirement Plan Wellness Center *Eligibility based on meeting required service period 2025 ICUBA Benefits Guide_St Leo"
    },
    "https://saintleo.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/University-Campus/Campus-Safety-Officer_R6655": {
      "title": "Campus Safety Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary The Campus Safety Officer is a uniformed, unarmed, Florida Class “D” licensed security professional who protects the life, safety, and property of Saint Leo University students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Officers provide visible patrol, access control, event support, and first response to medical, fire, and safety incidents, 24 hours a day, 365 days a year. Officers serve as approachable, community-oriented representatives of the University and carry out their duties consistent with Saint Leo’s Catholic Benedictine values of community, respect, and hospitality. Officers are not sworn law enforcement officers. They hold no greater legal authority than a private citizen and coordinate with the Pasco County Sheriff’s Office (PCSO), which has primary law enforcement jurisdiction over the campus, for any incident that exceeds that authority. Job Description Patrol and Access Control   Conduct foot, golf cart, and marked-vehicle patrol of assigned zones, including building and lock checks, residence hall access-control procedures, and documented checks of the Saint Leo Academy residential area.  Provide escort services, parking and traffic direction, and welfare checks, including missing-student protocols.  Verify identification of unfamiliar persons, and issue University trespass warnings in coordination with PCSO.  Emergency and Incident Response   Respond first to fire alarms, intrusion alarms, and medical emergencies; provide first aid, CPR, and AED care within training and certification until Fire Rescue, EMS, or PCSO arrives.  Respond to fights, alcohol- and substance-related incidents, and mental health crises using verbal de-escalation first, and summon PCSO whenever a weapon, felony, serious injury, or situation beyond private-person authority is involved.  Support active-threat, lockdown, bomb-threat, and severe weather procedures, following PCSO direction and the University’s emergency notification protocols.  Provide a clear verbal handoff to responding PCSO deputies and preserve the scene.  Use of Force and Legal Compliance   Use only the minimum objectively reasonable force, as defined by the University’s Use of Force Policy and Florida law, and de-escalate at the earliest safe opportunity. Officers never carry firearms and never use or threaten deadly force.  Carry and use OC spray and restraints only while current in certification, and disengage and summon PCSO when a situation cannot be safely resolved.  Event Support   Staff athletic contests, commencement, orientation, move-in/move-out, concerts, and other campus events, maintaining a visible, approachable presence and assisting with crowd flow, access points, and rapid response.  Minors and Special Populations   Follow heightened-duty-of-care procedures for Saint Leo Academy students, who are minors, including de-escalation as the required first response and release of minors only to authorized persons.  Report suspected abuse or neglect of any minor immediately to the Florida Abuse Hotline as a mandatory reporter, in parallel with internal notification.  Documentation, Equipment, and Training   Write accurate, timely incident, use-of-force, trespass, alarm, and shift reports; submit a Use of Force Report before the end of shift for any force at Level 4 (mechanical restraint) or above.  Inspect the duty belt, patrol vehicle, and golf cart at the start of every shift, restock used supplies, and tag deficient equipment out of service.  Complete the 80-hour Field Training Officer program before solo patrol and a minimum of 40 hours of in-service training every calendar year.  Wear the issued uniform and University ID visibly while on duty and meet grooming standards. Perform other duties as assigned.  AUTHORITY AND LIMITATIONS   Campus Safety Officers operate as a licensed private security function under Chapter 493, Florida Statutes. Officers may detain a person they directly witness committing a felony or breach of the peace, using reasonable non-deadly force, for the sole purpose of holding the person until PCSO arrives. Officers may not make formal arrests, conduct searches or seizures beyond those available to any private citizen, or pursue fleeing persons into traffic or unreasonable danger.  REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS   Current, unrestricted Florida Class “D” Security Officer License (FDACS), verified before an offer of employment and maintained through each two-year renewal.  Satisfactory criminal history background check, reference verification, and University suitability screening.  Ability to obtain and maintain CPR/AED/First Aid, OC spray, and restraint certifications during training; no Officer may work a solo post with an expired certification.  Valid driver’s license and the ability to be certified to operate the patrol vehicle and golf carts.   High school diploma or equivalent.   Ability to communicate clearly by radio and in writing, write clear reports, and remain calm and courteous under pressure.  Willingness to work 12-hour day or night shifts on a rotating squad schedule, including weekends, holidays, special events, and inclement-weather activations.  For Officers assigned to the Saint Leo Academy residential area: Level 2 background screening under Chapter 435 and Section 1012.32, Florida Statutes.  Preferred   Experience in security, law enforcement, military, or campus safety, particularly in a residential college or school setting.  Training in de-escalation, mental health crisis intervention, or Clery Act and Title IX reporting.  Commitment to serving a diverse student population, including international and first-generation students, in keeping with the University’s Benedictine values. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS AND WORK ENVIRONMENT   Work is performed outdoors and indoors in all weather and at all hours. The role requires extended periods of standing, walking, and driving; the ability to respond quickly on foot; the physical ability to perform first aid and CPR; and the ability to apply defensive and control techniques as trained. Officers must be able to wear the standard uniform and duty belt for an entire 12-hour shift. Reasonable accommodations will be made for qualified individuals with disabilities in accordance with applicable law.  ENVIRONMENT:   The work environment characteristics described here are a representation of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.  The term “qualified individual with a disability” means an individual with a disability who, with or without reasonable accommodation, can perform the essential functions of this position. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to communicate professionally in person, over the telephone, through email and other electronic means, move about the office and University, handle various type of media and equipment, and visually or otherwise identify, observe and assess.   The employee is occasionally required to lift up to 10 pounds unless otherwise specified in the job description. NOTICE: The intent of this job description is to provide a representation of the types of duties and responsibilities that will be required of positions given this title and shall not be construed as a declaration of the total specific duties and responsibilities of any particular position.  Employees may be directed to perform job-related tasks other than those specifically presented in this description.  Saint Leo University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and embraces diversity as a critical step in ensuring employee, student and graduate success.  Why Work at Saint Leo? What it’s Like to Work Here:  Ask our employees and the one word they’d use to describe working at Saint Leo University is “Community.” Our team members all share the Saint Leo core values, positive attitudes, and problem-solving abilities, enabling them to provide excellent student centered service. Our mission is educating and preparing students for life and leadership in a challenging world.  Thank you for your interest in joining the Saint Leo PRIDE! We are committed to providing our employees with the support they need. At Saint Leo, we offer an array of medical, dental, and vision packages as well as several add-on perks to make your benefits package truly customizable to you and your family needs. Available benefits based on employment status (Full Time vs Part Time). FREE Tuition - Employee, Spouse, and Dependents* Tuition Exchange Opportunity - Dependent of Employees* Generous Paid Leave - Sick, Vacation, and Holidays Comprehensive Group Health Plan (Medical, Dental, and Vision) Group Medical Plan includes Teledoc, Surgery Plus, Wellness Incentive Program and more! 100% Employer-Funded Health Reimbursement Account 100% Employer-Paid Short Term Disability Insurance 100% Employer-Funded Employee Assistance Program (healthcare and dependent options) Employer-provided life insurance Discounted On-Campus Dining Meal Plans Nationwide Pet Insurance Flexible Spending Accounts 403b Retirement Plan Wellness Center *Eligibility based on meeting required service period 2025 ICUBA Benefits Guide_St Leo"
    },
    "https://saintleo.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/University-Campus/Cohn-Visiting-Chair-in-Jewish-Thought--Assistant-Director-of-the-Center-for-Catholic-Jewish-Studies_R6505": {
      "title": "Cohn Visiting Chair in Jewish Thought, Assistant Director of the Center for Catholic-Jewish Studies",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary The Cohn Visiting Chair in Jewish Thought/Assistant Director of the CCJS position brings a Jewish scholar specializing in Jewish thought to Saint Leo University’s Center for Catholic-Jewish Studies (CCJS). It is made possible by the generosity of Maureen and Douglas Cohn, and it establishes the regular presence of a Jewish scholarly voice on interreligious issues in the Tampa Bay community and beyond, something which is needed in the region. The Cohn Visiting Chair in Jewish Thought/Assistant Director of the CCJS position is a one-year visiting appointment with the possibility of renewal as a full-time faculty member in the Department of Theology and Religion; and as Assistant Director of the CCJS. The position is devoted to scholarly research and teaching focused on Jewish thought as it relates to Christianity, and contemporary challenges. The CCJS welcomes diverse approaches to Catholic-Jewish Studies including historical, dialogical, comparative, and theological. It also collaborates with the CCJS director and local religious leaders to organize, coordinate, and lead interreligious education programs on campus and in the local community. The Cohn Visiting Chair allows students, faculty, and members of the community to significantly deepen their understanding of Judaism by having direct and regular access to a specialist in Jewish thought. The Cohn Visiting Chair engages members of the Tampa Bay Jewish Community, including lay leaders, synagogue rabbis, and non-affiliated Jews by creating interactive dialogue and community-focused events and programs. The position puts scholarship on Jewish thought and culture in dialogue with other religions and contemporary challenges on the Saint Leo campus, in the local community, and among scholars of Christian-Jewish relations. The position directly reports to the Director of the CCJS and to the VPAA. Job Description Duties and Tasks: The Cohn Visiting Chair in Jewish Thought/Assistant Director of the CCJS for the upcoming 27-28 Academic year, takes on the following responsibilities during each academic year of residence: 1) Organize and lead an interfaith education program for the local community; 2) teach a series of spring educational workshops for the local community; 3) teach one undergraduate course per semester at Saint Leo University; 4) design an online course in Jewish thought for Saint Leo University.   REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES:   Knowledge: PhD in the field of Theology and/or Religious Studies by the time of appointment (ABD may be considered).  A commitment to Catholic-Jewish studies and interreligious dialogue. Broad knowledge of the history of Jewish religious, philosophical, and ethical thought.  Experience in interacting with Jewish Community members and institutions, and a demonstrated ability to connect with Jews and Christians of all backgrounds, denominations, and affiliations. A compelling research agenda that promises significant work in the field.  Competence or experience relevant to coordinating academic programs, including implementing event programming logistics from start to finish, and coordinating with CCJS staff. Competence in teaching a range of courses in Judaism. A special interest in the study of Judaism’s relationship to Christianity is preferred.  REQUIRED DOCUMENTS In addition to your curriculum vitae, the following documents are required for consideration. Please be sure to check the email under which you applied for important instructions on completing remaining steps, including uploading documents in the second step of the application packet process as follows: Cover Letter Teaching Philosophy - (500 words or less), should highlight how your teaching philosophy and practices fit the Mission and Values of Saint Leo University. Three (3) Letters of Recommendation – Please note that letters of recommendation will be requested if an applicant is invited to the interview stage. Recommendation letters can be mailed to Academic Affairs at the address stated below or mailed directly to matthew.tapie@saintleo.edu TRANSCRIPTS Official transcripts are required for all adjuncts and all final full-time faculty candidates Official transcripts for Master, Graduate, and Doctorate degrees are required to complete your application packet and are to be issued directly to Saint Leo University from the respective education institution.* Transcripts that are “Issued to Student” or issued to another institution are not accepted. Digital and/or electronic transcripts cannot be accepted at this time. World Education Services (WES) Evaluation – A certified evaluation and translation from World Education Services (WES) is required for foreign transcripts and/or any and all degrees obtained from international universities. Expenses for official transcripts are the responsibility of the applicant. Please have transcripts and certified evaluations mailed to: Attn: Veronica Mantegna Academic Affairs – MC 2006 Saint Leo University PO Box 6665 Saint Leo, Florida 33574   ENVIRONMENT:     The work environment characteristics described here are a representation of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.  The term “qualified individual with a disability” means an individual with a disability who, with or without reasonable accommodation, can perform the essential functions of this position.   While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to communicate professionally in person, over the telephone, through email and other electronic means, move about the office and University, handle various type of media and equipment, and visually or otherwise identify, observe and assess.   The employee is occasionally required to lift up to 10 pounds unless otherwise specified in the job description.   NOTICE: The intent of this job description is to provide a representation of the types of duties and responsibilities that will be required of positions given this title and shall not be construed as a declaration of the total specific duties and responsibilities of any particular position.  Employees may be directed to perform job-related tasks other than those specifically presented in this description.  Saint Leo University is an Equal Opportunity Employer and embraces diversity as a critical step in ensuring employee, student and graduate success.    Why Work at Saint Leo? What it’s Like to Work Here:  Ask our employees and the one word they’d use to describe working at Saint Leo University is “Community.” Our team members all share the Saint Leo core values, positive attitudes, and problem-solving abilities, enabling them to provide excellent student centered service. Our mission is educating and preparing students for life and leadership in a challenging world.  Thank you for your interest in joining the Saint Leo PRIDE! We are committed to providing our employees with the support they need. At Saint Leo, we offer an array of medical, dental, and vision packages as well as several add-on perks to make your benefits package truly customizable to you and your family needs. Available benefits based on employment status (Full Time vs Part Time). FREE Tuition - Employee, Spouse, and Dependents* Tuition Exchange Opportunity - Dependent of Employees* Generous Paid Leave - Sick, Vacation, and Holidays Comprehensive Group Health Plan (Medical, Dental, and Vision) Group Medical Plan includes Teledoc, Surgery Plus, Wellness Incentive Program and more! 100% Employer-Funded Health Reimbursement Account 100% Employer-Paid Short Term Disability Insurance 100% Employer-Funded Employee Assistance Program (healthcare and dependent options) Employer-provided life insurance Discounted On-Campus Dining Meal Plans Nationwide Pet Insurance Flexible Spending Accounts 403b Retirement Plan Wellness Center *Eligibility based on meeting required service period 2025 ICUBA Benefits Guide_St Leo"
