ry information and teaching materials as provided on the course syllabus. Submit final grades within three (3) days after the end of the term. Deliver in a professional manner course content for any assigned course(s) as specified by the master syllabus and/or as directed by the appropriate academic school dean, director, or chair. Meet all scheduled class meetings for the assigned period.  Be available to students before and after class for individual consultation. Cooperate in the dissemination of information to students. Abide by and uphold University policies and core values. Carry out instructor duties and responsibilities as provided on the website, handbook(s), and policies. Adjuncts are assigned to specific teaching locations and report to their location administrator as it pertains to daily operations as defined in the term-by-term contractual agreement but ultimately have responsibility to their discipline-specific department chair or director and/or school dean. Required/Minimum Qualification(s): A minimum of a Master’s degree in Music: Voice Performance, Doctoral degree in Voice Performance preferred. Responsibilities: 1 - At least two years teaching experience in general education music courses, private voice instruction 2 - Create a unified, comprehensive syllabus for private voice instruction 3- Able to customize lessons to suit individual student needs 4- Create, administer and evaluate, exams, papers, and/or projects a. Attend juries b. Respond to student question and/or class related issues. 5- Experience using Canvas Learning Management System 6- Available to perform in faculty recitals, regular concerts, and outreach concerts throughout the academic year Why Work at Saint Leo? What it’s Like to Work Here:  Ask our employees and the one word they’d use to describe working at Saint Leo University is “Community.” Our team members all share the Saint Leo core values, positive attitudes, and problem-solving abilities, enabling them to provide excellen